{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 610,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Everyone loves the idea of parallel universes\n- maybe it's the appeal of an ideal world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5100,
    "dDurationMs": 3699,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where you have second chances and things turn\nout differently - an alternate reality where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8799,
    "dDurationMs": 4431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you do get into Hogwarts and the Star Wars\nprequels aren't made and you finally plug"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13230,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in your asymmetric computer cord correctly\non the first try... but is there really a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 17240,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "place in science for such wistful speculation?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19800,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean, if \"the universe\" is everything that\nthere is, you can't have two versions of it,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 24610,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 25610,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Otherwise the pair would really be everything\nand what you started off calling the universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29110,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wasn't."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30110,
    "dDurationMs": 5110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem here is terminology: physicists\nspeaking informally often say \"universe\" when"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35220,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they really mean \"observable universe\" - that\nis, the part of the whole universe that we've"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39760,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so far been able to see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 41310,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it's perfectly fine to talk about multiple\ndifferent observable universes - for example,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 45930,
    "dDurationMs": 4350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an alien near the edge of OUR observable universe\nwill see parts of the Whole Universe that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50280,
    "dDurationMs": 6070,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we cannot yet see, but that's a well-understood\nquestion and not what physicists normally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56350,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "talk about when they discuss multiple observable\nuniverses, or \"multi-verses.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60550,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So let's cut to the chase: in physics, the\nword \"Multiverse\" normally refers to one of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64420,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "three distinct and largely unrelated proposed\nphysical models for the universe - none of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69240,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which has been tested or confirmed by experiment,\nby the way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71930,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The three \"multiverse\" models are:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73810,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Type 1) Bubble universes or baby black hole\nuniverses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77360,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the most straightforward kind of multiverse:\nthe basic idea is that perhaps there are other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81540,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parts of the universe which are so far away\nthat we will never see them (or are inside"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85280,
    "dDurationMs": 2810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "black holes so similarly we will never see\nthem)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88090,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This kind of model was created as an attempt\nto explain why our universe is so good at"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92380,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making stars and galaxies and black holes\nand life - as the argument goes, if each of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96820,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these separate mutually un-seeable \"bubbles\"\nin the universe had slightly different laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 101100,
    "dDurationMs": 4690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of physics, then by definition we could only\nexist in one that had the right physical laws"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105790,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to allow us to exist."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113070,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're not convinced by this logic, don't\nworry too much: there's not yet any experimental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117070,
    "dDurationMs": 2730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evidence for this kind of multiverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119800,
    "dDurationMs": 3170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Multiverse type 2) Membranes and extra dimensions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122970,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Inspired in part by the inability of the mathematics\nof string theory to predict the right number"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126890,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of dimensions for the universe in which we\nlive, string theorists proposed the idea that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130940,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perhaps what we think of as our universe is\nactually just a three-dimensional surface"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135170,
    "dDurationMs": 4050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "embedded within a larger super-universe with\n9 spatial dimensions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139220,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kind of like how each page of a newspaper\nis its own two-dimensional surface embedded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143040,
    "dDurationMs": 2010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "within our three-dimensional world."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145050,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And of course, if space had 9 dimensions rather\nthan three, there'd be plenty of space for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149800,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "other three-dimensional surfaces that appeared,\nlike ours, to be universes in their own right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 153950,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but, like the pages of a newspaper, were actually\npart of a bigger whole."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157700,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These kinds of surfaces are called \"membranes\"\nor \"branes\" for short."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161180,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as a reminder, there is not yet any experimental\nevidence for this kind of multiverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166300,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Multiverse type 3) The many-worlds picture\nof quantum mechanics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169960,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Surprisingly, physicists still don't fully\nunderstand how the collapse of the wavefunction"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173870,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in quantum mechanics happens, and the many-worlds\nhypothesis makes an attempt at explanation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178410,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by proposing that every possible alternate\ntimeline for the universe is real and they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182450,
    "dDurationMs": 2590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all happen in an ever-larger, ever-branching\nway."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185040,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like, a universal choose-your-own-adventure\nwhere every possible story happens!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189690,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If this were the case, we might not realize\nit because we'd be stuck living out just one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193220,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of the infinitely many possible lives available\nto us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196060,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In some ways, many-worlds is similar to the\nbubble multiverse model by proposing \"maybe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200600,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "anything that can happen, does."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202620,
    "dDurationMs": 3789,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we just happen to exist in the series\nof happenings that were necessary for us to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206409,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exist.\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207409,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you're still not convinced by this logic,\ndon't worry: there is not yet any experimental"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210769,
    "dDurationMs": 2431,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "evidence for this kind of multiverse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213200,
    "dDurationMs": 3390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course if you want to get imaginative,\nyou could also combine several of these models"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216590,
    "dDurationMs": 5011,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "together into a multi-multiverse... a new\nsuper-speculative model based, itself, on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221601,
    "dDurationMs": 2968,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "speculative and experimentally unconfirmed\nmodels."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224569,
    "dDurationMs": 3081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that's not to say we couldn't test these\nmultiverse hypotheses."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227650,
    "dDurationMs": 4010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, if our observable universe were\nreally just one of many disconnected bubbles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231660,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or membranes and if it happened to collide\nwith another bubble or membrane some time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235190,
    "dDurationMs": 3909,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the past, then that collision would certainly\nhave had some sort of effect on what we see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239099,
    "dDurationMs": 2261,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when we look up at the night sky."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241360,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand, the many-worlds interpretation\nmight be tested fairly soon since experimentalists"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246110,
    "dDurationMs": 3989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are becoming increasingly able to manipulate\nand control ever-larger quantum mechanical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250099,
    "dDurationMs": 4171,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "systems in their labs - systems that approach\nthe line between the quantum realm and our"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254270,
    "dDurationMs": 1529,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "everyday experience."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255799,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So as always, we must remember that physics\nis science, not philosophy; and in our attempts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260099,
    "dDurationMs": 3910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to explain the universe that we observe, we\nhave to make claims that can in principle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264009,
    "dDurationMs": 31240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be tested - and then test them!"
    } ]
  } ]
}
